Z||000000||fierojunky||01-30-2001||03:11 PM||||my check engine light came on the other night - the cars still running great - its an 87 SE 6 cyl auto - i took it to the shop to get the code read and they said its EGR related - any suggestions on where to start?  Also - whats the damage if i keep running it?  Thanks!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-30-2001||03:18 PM||||Do a search on error code 32.  A very common error which can be a pain to track down.  Usually vaccuum leak to the EGR selinoid, egr tube or emission equipment on the car.  Mine comes on intermittantly for the last year, my car runs great.  I'm changing vaccuum lines one at a time to see if I can track it down.  Of course it may take several days or weeks to get the code to pop on again.  If the car is running ok, good performance and good gas milage, there should be no adverse effects.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierojunky||01-30-2001||03:38 PM||||thanks for the quick reply - my comes on all the time after only like 10 minutes of running - so mabey its the solenoid not the tubes?||||reg||11
Z||000003||My7Fieros||01-30-2001||06:06 PM||||If its a code 32, then Id just replace the egr and tube..a pretty easy task. <BR>You dont need to take your car in to have the codes read...simply pull off the black cover where the cig. lighter is, and use a paper clip. Stick on end in the lower right corner square, and the other in the square right next to it while the key is in the "on" position (but the car ISNT running)..itll go "flash"...."flash flash" three times..then itll send the code (like for yours it'd go "flash flash flash"....."flash flash"....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
